EU finance ministers meeting in  Luxembourg want to put flesh on the  bones of Europe's investment and girls  plans ministers will discuss concrete  measures to be presented by the  Commission and the European Investment  Bank to boost investment in projects  which could generate growth and jobs  ministers are also said to discuss a  commission communication on research and  innovation as sources of renewed growth  in the field of Taxation the council is  expected to reach political agreement on  a proposal aimed at the neighbouring  member states to better combat tax fraud  and tax evasion the idea is to extend  the scope of the mandatory automatic  exchange of information between tax  administration's to include also  dividends capital gains other financial  income and account balances ministers  will also debate a proposal to  restructure the taxation of energy  products and electricity to promote  energy efficiency and a greater use of  renewable sources the council will be  briefed by the Commission on the  preparation of implementing legislation  on contributions to be paid by banks to  resolution funds established under  recently agreed rules on bank resolution  under the new rules banks will have to  make annual contributions which will be  calculated on the basis of their  liabilities excluding own funds and  cover deposits and adjusted for risk
 

